
== §0 — SPEC INTEGRITY AND THE NON-NEGOTIABLE PIPELINE ==
  ✓ the browser spec is byte-identical to acs_render.json
  ✓ the compiler version is declared
  ✓ the pipeline runs model to image and never the reverse
  ✓ the base render is declared the geometry authority
  ✓ only the model feeds the model hash
  ✓ every one of the eleven output types is declared
  ✓ no photorealistic generator is claimed as shipped
  ✓ the four verification classes are declared and distinguished
  ✓ stub output is explicitly not a rendering pass

== §1 — THE RENDER REQUEST IS TYPED, PINNED AND PRESENTATION ONLY ==
  ✓ a well-formed request is accepted
  ✓ the request is pinned to the model hash
  ✓ the request is pinned to the revision
  ✓ the request declares it never writes to the model
  ✓ every declared request field is present
  ✓ an unknown view type is refused, not defaulted
  ✓ an unknown quality is refused
  ✓ an unknown theme is refused
  ✓ an unknown lighting preset is refused
  ✓ an oversized resolution is refused
  ✓ a resolution is only recorded when it was accepted
  ✓ the same inputs produce the same request id
  ✓ a different theme produces a different request id

== §3 — THE DETERMINISTIC PATH NEVER DEPENDS ON AI ==
  ✓ a camera is solved with no provider present
  ✓ a deterministic descriptor exists without AI
  ✓ the deterministic descriptor claims no engineering authority
  ✓ with no provider the base render remains the output
  ✓ a provider failure produces a real issue, never a blank output
  ✓ a provider failure touches nothing in the model

== §4-§7 — MATERIALS ARE APPEARANCE, NEVER ENGINEERING ==
